# What ships in the .vsix. See spec Section 10.
#
# Everything is excluded, and the handful of files that ship are named back in
# below. That order matters: vsce applies negations as a union at the end rather
# than in sequence, so a broad `!out/**` followed by carve-outs does not work —
# the carve-outs lose. Naming each file that ships is the only arrangement that
# stays correct, and it has the side benefit that new junk at the repository
# root cannot leak into a release by default.
**

!package.json
!media/icon.svg

# The bundles esbuild produces. dev.js is the browser harness for developing the
# renderer without an extension host, and has no business in an installed
# extension. The .map files are excluded for the same reason.
!out/extension.js
!out/webview.js
!out/setup.js
!out/style.css

# Workflow definitions stay bundled: they are what the tool standardises.
!workflows/*.json

# Prompt templates stay bundled because they are the per-file fallback for any
# template a team has not supplied, so they must remain good. See Section 16.
!prompts/**/*.md

# The layout a team copies to make its own content folder, shipped so it can be
# copied out of an installed extension. See Sections 16 and 17.
!examples/content-template/README.md
!examples/content-template/config/*.json
